Hooray!  My first ascension!  I started playing at the beginning of the
summer, and took a 2 month hiatus.  I started again while waiting for
my job to start, and decided (after about 50 games with random classes)
that i really liked archaeologists.  Don't ask me why, i just felt like
Indy, with the fedora & the whip.  Indiana, of course, was always my
dogs name.

So this game went real well.  I stopped in minetown and found a blessed
magic lamp for the low, low price of 50 zm.  50 zm for a wish is deal
of the century, so i blew it on some GDSM.  I found a luckstone before
the bottom, so I went back up and did Soko, getting a BoH, which was so
useful because arkeys really aren't so strong.  But on the way back
down I found some gauntlets of power, so, hey, win-win.  I had a
sac-fest in minetown and got grayswandir, which i quickly advanced.  I
ended up with a ton of luckstones, too, by the time i went back to the
main branch.

Down and down...i had really bad luck with thrones, they always
vanished before doing anything nice, but one of them hooked me up with
*two* genocides *AND* a wish.  I used the two genocides to genocide
both types of mind-flayers (as a dwarf, i didn't use the blessed scroll
on "h" -- that mistake ONCE was enough :), and picked up my speed boots
there.

my quest was ridiculously easy.  A bones file was right on the 1st
non-special level, with another BoH and some great potions and gear to
fill out my kit -- the +7 GS took care of the Minion of Huehotl lickidy
split, and ludios was a snap.  The castle was a little odd, because i
read a confused scroll of taming and tamed half the baddies, who all
promptly fell down to the valley of death.  A little alchemy and i had
a shweet max HP (350) and i went through gehennom, GS & my silver sabre
beating the hell out of everyone.

After being phenomenally nervous about the ascension run, it wasn't so
bad as i thought it'd be -- Rodney wasn't too much of a pest, the Arc
quest artifact found all the magic portals, and each plane was really
pretty easy.  The riders fell to my /oD (except Death, who i didn't
have to face), and i ascended with 2 wishes still in my /oWishing.

here's hoping everyone else has equally good RNG luck :)

